---
import ProjectLayout from '../../layouts/ProjectLayout.astro';
import Armor from '../../components/react/Armor.jsx';
import Carousel from '../../components/react/Carousel.jsx';
import '../../styles/project.css';
const slides=[{src:'/images/projects/volkihar-knight/slide-1.jpg',alt:'A character wearing the black Volkihar Knight armor set.'},{src:'/images/projects/volkihar-knight/slide-2.jpg',alt:'A close view of the custom gauntlet design.'},{src:'/images/projects/volkihar-knight/slide-3.jpg',alt:'A character wearing the red armor set.'}];
---
<ProjectLayout title="Volkihar Knight" description="A lore-friendly armor mod for The Elder Scrolls V: Skyrim, released on PC and Xbox One with over one million downloads." roles={['3D Modelling','Texturing','Graphic Design']} background="/images/projects/volkihar-knight.jpg" accent="#ead68d">
  <section class="project-section"><div class="project-content"><div class="project-media"><img src="/images/projects/volkihar-knight/banner.jpg" width="1100" height="600" alt="A dark elf wearing the Volkihar Knight armor." /></div><div class="project-copy"><h2>From a gap in the game</h2><div class="prose"><p>The Volkihar faction offered no heavy-armor option. The mod combines and reshapes existing visual language into a set that feels native to Skyrim’s world.</p></div></div></div></section>
  <section class="project-section" data-tone="soft"><div class="project-content"><div class="project-copy"><h2>Armor design</h2><div class="prose"><p>Meshes from faction clothing and heavy plate were combined in 3DS Max, then supported by custom textures designed to keep the set cohesive across its variations.</p><p>The original model asset is requested only when this section approaches the viewport.</p></div></div><div class="graphics-stage"><Armor client:visible /></div></div></section>
  <section class="project-section"><div class="project-content"><div class="project-copy"><h2>Identity design</h2><div class="prose"><p>The monogram uses custom angular lettering balanced with Trajan, echoing the visual character of Skyrim’s title treatment.</p></div></div><div class="project-media"><img src="/images/projects/volkihar-knight/book.png" width="960" height="600" loading="lazy" alt="A concept book showing the armor and identity sketches." /></div></div></section>
  <section class="project-section" data-tone="soft"><div class="project-content"><Carousel client:visible images={slides} label="Volkihar Knight armor gallery" /></div></section>
  <section class="project-section"><div class="project-content"><div class="project-copy"><h2>Featured in Enderal</h2><div class="prose"><p>The armor was later included in Enderal, the award-winning standalone Skyrim mod, as the Wandering Mage armor set.</p></div></div><div class="project-media"><img src="/images/projects/volkihar-knight/enderal.jpg" width="1920" height="1080" loading="lazy" alt="Characters in Enderal overlooking a distant city." /></div></div></section>
</ProjectLayout>
